RF.put("questb:b11",{"8171":{"id":8171,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the Arathi Basin mine, lumber mill, blacksmith and stable, and then return to Deathmaster Dwire in Hammerfall.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nStable Assaulted","desc":"As you no doubt have heard, the League of Arathor is sending large numbers of troops into Arathi Basin. Eager for food and supplies, these Alliance fools are intent to take and control the rich resources there. We must show them that Arathi will never again be a home for humans!\nGo to Arathi Basin and assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the stables. Pull down the enemies' banners, declaring those territories for the Horde.\nGo, ‹name›. Report back to me when this task is complete.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+200 reputation with The Defilers","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.3,"y":29.7,"n":"Deathmaster Dwire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"651":{"id":651,"t":"Stones of Binding","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather the Burning Key, the Cresting Key and the Thundering Key from the Stone of West Binding, the Stone of East Binding and the Stone of Outer Binding.\nBring them to the Stone of Inner Binding.\nBurning Key Stone of West Binding , Burning Exile 0.1 %\nCresting Key Stone of East Binding\nThundering Key Stone of Outer Binding","desc":"Four Stones of Binding are scattered throughout Arathi. These stones keep me pinned beneath the earth.\nTo unlock them you must unlock the strongest: the Stone of Inner Binding. And to do that, you must gather keys from the other three.\nThese stones are watched by guardians, but if you are clever, or lucky, you may find ways to banish them.","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"This is the Stone of Inner Binding. It is the strongest of the binding stones and must be unlocked for the others to open.","done":"<Myzrael speaks through the stone.>\nYou have done it! You opened the Stones of Binding! I can feel the shackles about me loosen, and freedom draws ever closer.\nYou are a noble ‹class›, ‹name›. My rescuer!","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":84.3,"y":31,"n":"Iridescent Shards","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":36.2,"y":57.4,"n":"Stone of Inner Binding","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6571":{"id":6571,"t":"Warsong Supplies","lv":27,"min":22,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect the Warsong Supplies: Warsong Saw Blades, Logging Rope, Warsong Oil, and the Warsong Axe Shipment for Locke Okarr in Splintertree Post.\nWarsong Saw Blades\nWarsong Axe Shipment Warsong Axe Shipment\nWarsong Oil Warsong Oil\nLogging Rope Thistlefur Pathfinder 10 % , Thistlefur Avenger 10 % , Thistlefur Shaman 10 % , Thistlefur Den Watcher 10 % and 4 more","desc":"We are in short supply of a few items at the Warsong lumber camp!\nPixel at Splintertree Post has our shipment of saw blades. It'll take a trip to Booty Bay to pick up a crate of axes from Wharfmaster Lozgil.\nOur shipment of oil and rope will be more difficult. The rope was pilfered by the Thistlefur and Foulweald furbolgs, and the satyrs intercepted the delivery of the oil and are now using it for detestable rituals in Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian!\nCan you help me?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWarsong Sash Warsong Boots Warsong Gauntlets\nExperience: 2,750\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I hope you can come through with the supplies!","done":"Excellent, ‹name›. You've saved me a lot of work!\nBut don't think that I'm not grateful!\nAshenvale Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":71.4,"y":67.6,"n":"Locke Okarr","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"971":{"id":971,"t":"Knowledge in the Deeps","lv":23,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,550 experience instead of 2,750, 2.38 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring the Lorgalis Manuscript to Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern in Ironforge.\nLorgalis Manuscript Pitted Iron Chest , Document Chest","desc":"As you might know, I collect lore. Old lore. Powerful lore. Lore that opens doorways, and lore that can awaken Those Who Sleep.\nThere are rumors of an old piece of lore, the Lorgalis Manuscript, at the bottom of Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale. That place is the old dwelling of long-dead elves. Elves who held great knowledge before their city fell to ruin.\nSearch Blackfathom Deeps for the manuscript. Do this, and I will not forget it. Not even after ... the end days.","rew":"You will receive:\nSustaining Ring\nExperience: 6,550\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The journey to Ashenvale is long, and your task is not easy. But if you get me the manuscript, ‹name›...then your reward will be great.","done":"You found the manuscript! What a joyous day this is! Copies will be made and distributed, and the ancient knowledge of Lorgalis will finally be known to my brothers and sisters!\nYour service to us is more than you know, ‹name›. But I hope that this gift shows you the gratitude we extend to our allies.\nDun Morogh Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Gerrig Bonegrip","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"97931":{"id":97931,"t":"Camping 101 first aid","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Vira Younghoof in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your first aid skill to 20","desc":"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a ‹class›.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.8,"y":60.8,"n":"Vira Younghoof","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94331":{"id":94331,"t":"Craftsmans writ huge thorium battleaxe","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Huge Thorium Battleaxe\nHuge Thorium Battleaxe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Huge Thorium Battleaxe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Huge Thorium Battleaxe Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94331","cats":["crafting"]},"94251":{"id":94251,"t":"Craftsmans writ phoenix pants","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Phoenix Pants\nPhoenix Pants","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Phoenix Pants, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"You come get 'da voodoo?","done":"Hmm.\nI think you be a lil' lost if you think these gaudy pants were somethin' I be after.\nI'll take 'dem off your hands anyway. You never know when another adventurer be needin' a new pair!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.6,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7931":{"id":7931,"t":"5 Tickets - Minor Darkmoon Prize","lv":60,"min":15,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nMinor Darkmoon Prize","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (5)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"4811":{"id":4811,"t":"The Red Crystal","lv":14,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel east of Auberdine and look for a large, red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain range. Report back what you find to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"Hostile moonkin roam in ever increasing numbers to our east. They once were thought to be gentle, almost mystical creatures. While some continue to hold reverence for them, the safety of Auberdine forces me to keep a more realistic view.\nI've received reports that moonkin are being drawn to a large red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain range. No one has any idea what that crystal is, or even if it really exists. I want you to locate it over there and report back to me what you find.","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"What do you have to report on that red crystal? Does it even really exist?","done":"So the crystal exists, ‹name›? Fascinating... anyway, your task has been well executed; good work!\nWhat exactly is this crystal? This is but a single question in a sea of questions. Another question that comes to mind is why the moonkin would be drawn to this object? Is the crystal benign in nature, or does it hold a more sinister purpose?\nI have many more questions, but we're going to need to examine that crystal closely to get some answers.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":43.4,"n":"Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"4731":{"id":4731,"t":"Beached Sea Turtle","lv":19,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 725 experience instead of 750, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Take the Strangely Marked Box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nStrangely Marked Box\nProvided: Strangely Marked Box","desc":"Another set of sea turtle remains lie beached on the coastline. This set of remains has an abandoned carriage half buckled to the turtle's shell. Perhaps this creature was driven to the shoreline by unknown beings rather than beaching itself as some of the other remains suggested. Powerful Greymist murlocs have made the carcass of this creature their current home.\nIn the carriage, you find a box with strange markings on it; perhaps Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine can make sense of it.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 725\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello again, ‹name›. The work you have done on behalf of the Temple of the Moon has been outstanding. Are we to be blessed with more of your effort on our behalf?","done":"I have heard of the kinds of carriages found on the back of that turtle. Those I do believe are naga carriages, used both in battle and in transportation of their supplies on to land. The markings on the box you found are of the naga; perhaps the creature you discovered was killed as it was heading further south... to Ashenvale maybe?\nI will be sure to send this box to Darnassus with the rest of your discoveries. This is for you - thank you again for your assistance.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":31.7,"y":83.7,"n":"Beached Sea Turtle","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"731":{"id":731,"t":"The Absent Minded Prospector","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Prospector Remtravel as he searches for the mysterious fossil, then return to Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine.","desc":"So then, Hollee... oh that's right, you are not Hollee. Where's Hollee?\nBah, that's beside the point. We must find that stone brush... I mean the mysterious fossil! We must find that fossil. The Explorers' League in Darnassus will want some indication as to what I've been doing.\nLet me know when you are ready and we will hunt down that brush.... I mean fossil! We shall find something in writing to satisfy the League.\nSo are you ready yet?","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Is the prospector alive?","done":"Thank the stars Prospector Remtravel is safe! I told you he was absent minded. I can't believe he insisted on staying there with all of those horrible creatures lurking about.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":35.7,"y":83.7,"n":"Prospector Remtravel","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":41.8,"n":"Archaeologist Hollee","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98891":{"id":98891,"t":"Conflict at darkspear islands","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.\nGo, show them the might of the horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Raiders\nLevel 59 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 55 57 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 98891","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1371":{"id":1371,"t":"Gizmo for Warug","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Schematic: Centaur Banner Deployment Device, Schematic: Hoof-Shaped Foot Pedal.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring an Advanced Target Dummy to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\nAdvanced Target Dummy\nReach 3000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","desc":"Long ago, a little gnome came to Desolace. He had horses and a cart, and the cart held strange things. Funny things. Things that burned different colors. Things that moved and weren't alive. I killed the little gnome, but before that... he made me laugh.\nI kept my favorite thing from his cart. It was a human made of wood and it waved at me until I hit it and broke it.\nI want a new one. Get me a new one!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSchematic: Hoof-Shaped Foot Pedal Schematic: Centaur Banner Deployment Device\nNew in Forever: Schematic: Hoof-Shaped Foot Pedal, Schematic: Centaur Banner Deployment Device.\nExperience: 2,050","back":"If you are not our enemy, then you will do what I ask!","done":"Yes, this is what I had! I will make it move again. It makes me laugh!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":75,"y":68.2,"n":"Warug","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"92811":{"id":92811,"t":"Economic warfare","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"5 Carved Centaur Totem\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 92811","cats":["desolace"]},"5931":{"id":5931,"t":"Back to Darnassus","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Darnassus and speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave.","desc":"The time has come for us to part ways, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me. Mathrengyl Bearwalker walks truly in balance with nature, even as he dwells precariously close to where the balance has faltered. Listen to his instructions, and you will soon complete your first lessons into your role as a protector of balance.\nGo now, young one. We shall meet again.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Welcome back, ‹name›. I sense that your first meeting with the Great Bear Spirit is the same as it is with all druids when they first start down the path of the Claw... a little bewildering, but very intense. I know it was that way with me.\nThe Great Bear Spirit has been a part of Azeroth as long as Azeroth has existed in the heavens. We have come to rely on its wisdom and its power to fuel our purpose. Now, the time has now come for your first test of this purpose. Listen closely...\nMoonglade Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"98731":{"id":98731,"t":"Blessings of the great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","desc":"Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further. I do hope we meet again someday.\nMay the shadows forever hide you and your foes easily fall prey to your claws, young one.","done":"<Dendrite makes another invisible gesture in the air above him as you approach. Another aura of power comes over him, and he smiles ever so slightly.>\nI sense the cunning and ferocity of the cat within you that was not present when I sent you to meet the Great Cat Spirit. In your eyes I can sense you now understand the stealth and speed needed to adopt this nature.\nNow you may learn to focus your cunning and adopt the true nature of the cat and call upon its spirit.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":54.5,"y":74.8,"n":"Great Cat Spirit","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"9051":{"id":9051,"t":"Toxic Test","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stab a Devilsaur with the Devilsaur Barb. Return to Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater when you have completed this task.\nProvided: Devilsaur Barb","desc":"The toxin you helped me create is for a special purpose. The great devilsaurs of the crater make it dangerous to hunt and difficult for me to survive. Even if I possessed the necessary strength, killing a devilsaur simply allows another to move into its territory.\nTake this poisoned barb and stab it deep into a living devilsaur. The toxin should pacify the creature, though I do not know how quickly...","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Were you able to pacify the great beast?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. You are brave and wise.\nTell me, how did the devilsaur react to the toxin?","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"99051":{"id":99051,"t":"Threat from below","lv":11,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 9 Naga Spinefins.\n9 Naga Spinefin","desc":"It wouldn't be the first time those snakes bothered us. They need to be taught that their presence is not tolerated here.\nFind where their scouts are setting up camp and slaughter them. Bring me back their fins as proof. We need to act fast to make sure they understand.","back":"Hopefully those snake scum aren't giving you trouble?","done":"Hopefully that sends them packing back to the north. I'll have some grunts keep an eye out for any stragglers or funny business.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Orgnil Soulscar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"251":{"id":251,"t":"Translate Abercrombie's Note","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Letter to Ello to Sirra Von'Indi.\nLetter to Ello\nProvided: Letter to Ello","desc":"Take the note you gave me to Sirra Von'Indi. He's very learned in languages and ancient arts - if anyone here can translate this message, it's he.","rew":"Experience: 250","back":"A note from Abercrombie the hermit, eh? I don't know him, though if he lives out at the graveyard then I do know his brains have rotted out!","done":"<Sirra begins translating the note...>","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":71.9,"y":46.4,"n":"Lord Ello Ebonlocke","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Sirra Von'Indi","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"5211":{"id":5211,"t":"Defenders of Darrowshire","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Free 15 Darrowshire Spirits and return to Carlin Redpath.\nDarrowshire Spirits Freed : 0/ 15","desc":"Many of the defenders fell at the battle of Darrowshire. And many roam again as the ghastly servants of the Scourge! Find these poor souls and end their misery!\nHunt cannibal ghouls, gibbering ghouls and diseased flayers. Many of these fiends were once the good folk of Darrowshire and destroying their forms now will set their souls free.\nYou will find them in Plaguewood and Corin's Crossing, and in other Scourge strongholds of Eastern Plaguelands.","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"The poor defenders of Darrowshire cry out to me in my dreams, ‹name›. You must free them!","done":"It is good to hear you found the tortured souls of my brethren and freed them. My heart will weep less, knowing at least some of the defenders of Darrowshire no longer wallow in the vile subservience of the Scourge.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50,"n":"Carlin Redpath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9131":{"id":9131,"t":"Binding the Dreadnaught","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Dark Iron Scraps.\n30 Dark Iron Scraps Blackrock Raider 38.7 % , Blackrock Ambusher 35.3 % , Blackrock Battlemaster 35.2 % , Krom'Grul 34.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Have you ever seen Dreadnaught armor, ‹class›? No, of course you haven't. You're still a boy/girl - a tyke. Let me tell you, it is glorious.\nYou're probably asking yourself what any of this has to do with you, right? I'll tell you what, scrub; I need Dark Iron scraps and I'm willing to pay to get my hands on as many as possible.\nI need the scraps to put together sets of Dreadnaught for our champions. Bring me scraps and get paid.","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Dawn\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"<Korfax growls at you.>\nWhat do you want? Directions? I can provide those...","done":"This will do, for now. If you get more, you know where to find me.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9211":{"id":9211,"t":"The Ice Guard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 10 Insignia of the Crusade and 30 gold.\n10 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Ah, the Ice Guard. It is a thin sheen of protective magic that covers certain pieces of equipment. Those that do battle with creatures of frost and ice will gain increased protection from their attacks by using the Ice Guard.\nAs with all things the Wrathcaster creates, there is a price - a price that I will not lower, regardless of how much you whimper. Interested?","rew":"You will receive:\nIce Guard\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"If it were not for these Argent Dawn guards, you would be a stain upon this floor.","done":"<Mataus pockets the gold.>\nEnjoy the repair costs, ‹race›. Naxxramas is 'unkind' to the uninitiated.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"99131":{"id":99131,"t":"Baited for success","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return to Jason Mathers.","desc":"Tell Mathers he can come pick up the bait later today. I'll give him the rundown on the proper usage.\nHopefully he'll be able to sell his fish again soon. And we'll have less murlocs in this world.","done":"Poisoned bait? As long as the fish aren't going to eat it, that should work. I'll visit Remy later to pick it up.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Remy \"Two Times\"","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.4,"y":62.2,"n":"Jason Mathers","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"95771":{"id":95771,"t":"A taste of darkness","lv":10,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Scout through the Fargodeep Mine","rew":"You will receive:\nUnholy Icon\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\nLevel 10 , requires level 6 Difficulty 6 8 13 16 Side Both factions Quest ID 95771","cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"11":{"id":11,"t":"Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty","lv":10,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Painted Gnoll Armbands to Deputy Rainer at the Barracks.\n8 Painted Gnoll Armband Riverpaw Outrunner 40 % , Riverpaw Runt 40 %","desc":"Gnolls, brutish creatures with no decent business in these lands, have been seen along the borders of Elwynn Forest. A large pack of them, many more than we can handle alone, have infested the woods south of the guard tower yonder. Another group has infested the areas near Stone Cairn Lake to the east.\nThe Stormwind Army will commend whomever helps kill them. Bring me their painted gnoll armbands as proof of your deed.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMilitia Buckler Urchin's Pants\nExperience: 850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hail, ‹name›. Have you been killing Gnolls...?","done":"I see you've been busy! You have our thanks, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":24.2,"y":74.4,"n":"Deputy Rainer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3451":{"id":3451,"t":"Signal for Pickup","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Xiggs Fuselighter and get a Standard Issue Flare Gun from him in Ironforge.","desc":"Ah, so Tymor sent you, huh? Yeah, I owe him a favor or two. What's that? Why, that little devil. Yeah, I can help him out with that. So you'll need a flare gun and a location... easy enough.\nThere's a small island off the southern peninsula of Azshara that we've made a landing pad on. You take this flare gun, and use it there. I'll see your signal and come by to pick up this... whatever it is he wants.","rew":"You will receive:\nStandard Issue Flare Gun\nExperience: 500","done":"Here's my standard issue flare gun, and be patient after you fire off the gun--there are only a couple charges in one of these, and it might take me a minute to get to you depending on how far out to sea I am. Just look out to sea after you fire off the flare.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":36.3,"n":"Xiggs Fuselighter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"3371":{"id":3371,"t":"Dwarven Justice","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to the Searing Gorge and find Dorius's archaeology unit.","desc":"There is an empty, vacuous hole, where my heart used to be, ‹name›. The loss of Dorius is not one that I will soon recover from. I must see his final wish through - the perpetrators of this cold blooded murder must be brought to justice.\nReturn to the Searing Gorge and fulfill his last request: Free his men. The Dark Iron dwarves force their slaves to work in a sweltering mine called the Slag Pits. Search there for Dorius' men.","rew":"Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Forget about me, help the others.\nDun Morogh Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Curator Thorius","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":41.1,"y":25.6,"n":"Dying Archaeologist","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8651":{"id":8651,"t":"Ironband the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":21.5,"y":79,"n":"Elder Ironband","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8251":{"id":8251,"t":"Magic Dust","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Glittering Dust to Archmage Xylem.\n10 Glittering Dust Blood Elf Reclaimer 80 % , Blood Elf Surveyor 80 %","desc":"The blood elves in Azshara have developed a method for pulverizing the magical items they acquire. This glittering dust they produce differs from the components normally acquired by a disenchantment spell.\nWhen I sent my apprentice to trade for the dust, he was killed without hesitation. For that, they must pay.\nThe time for talk is over, ‹name›. Find the blood elves along the cliffs of Azshara and use more \"persuasive\" methods to acquire their glittering dust.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Have you the dust?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! It never ceases to amaze me how persuasive a volley of arcane missiles can be.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"91":{"id":91,"t":"Solomon's Law","lv":23,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Shadowhide Pendants to Bailiff Conacher in the Lakeshire Town Hall.\n10 Shadowhide Pendant Rohh the Silent 80 % , Lieutenant Fangore 80 % , Shadowhide Assassin 80 % , Shadowhide Warrior 80 % and 4 more","desc":"An enemy of Stormwind has taken up residence in the eastern foothills of Redridge. This wicked villain uses the Arcane to spread terror and misery upon our town and our people. Under the name, Morganth, he conducts his evil business.\nMorganth now controls the Shadowhide Gnoll Clan to perform his biddings. As stated by the Law of Lakeshire, aiding a criminal of the Kingdom is punishable by death.\nThese vile gnolls must be killed!\nTurn in 10 Shadowhide Pendants to me, and you shall be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 15 0 gold, 15 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Turn in 10 Shadowhide Pendants to me, and you shall be rewarded.","done":"The Court of Lakeshire recognizes your commitment to justice, ‹name›. By enforcing the laws of the Kingdom you have helped uphold the justice of the land.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.6,"y":44.3,"n":"Bailiff Conacher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8811":{"id":8811,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Stormwind.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.9,"y":32.2,"n":"Darnassus Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.4,"y":74.5,"n":"Officer Maloof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"97291":{"id":97291,"t":"Unending torment","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect a Toxic Skullcap from Tawny Grisette in the Trade Quarter, Blisterweed near the Herbalism Trainer, and Essence of Agony from the poison vendor in the Rogues' Quarter for Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.\nToxic Skullcap\nBlisterweed\nEssence of Agony","desc":"With the head reattached, all we need now is to bind it to the Dark Lady's will. This should not be a problem. The beast barely has brains left as it is after all the beatings it's taken.\nWe simply need to motivate it.\nFetch me a Toxic Skullcap from Miss Grisette in the Trade Quarter. Oh, and some Blisterweed from our local herbalist trainers, the Alliestars. Feel free to just take some, they owe me. And lastly a bit of Essence of Agony. Any old poison vendor should do.\nWe have a potion to make!","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650","back":"It will be ever so lovely to have our lost sheep returned to the fold, don't you think?","done":"These will do nicely. We will see how much bravado our honored guest retains after he is subjected to my masterpiece.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.4,"y":69.4,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron"]},"1051":{"id":1051,"t":"Vorrel's Revenge","lv":33,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Vorrel Sengutz's wedding ring to Monika Sengutz in Tarren Mill.\nVorrel's Wedding Ring Nancy Vishas","desc":"Even though my will is free, I can serve the Dark Lady no more. I feel my time on Azeroth has come to an end. My life force is shattered.\nInterrogator Vishas did this to me! Tortured me for weeks! Took my wedding ring and gave it to his wife. The bastard!\nRevenge... I want revenge!\nThe pompous fool bragged about his precious wife, Nancy, who lived along Lake Lordamere. Track the wench down, slay her and return my wedding ring to my wife, Monika in Tarren Mill.\nHeed my last wishes....","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMantle of Woe Grimsteel Cape\nYou will also receive:\nVorrel's Boots\nExperience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"What do you want, stranger?","done":"Vorrel led such a troubled existence. And what a good mate he was...\nDamn those filthy humans!\nVorrel is gone, never to enjoy undeath again. At least I can take solace in the revenge you took in his name. For that I thank you.\nNow let me be to mourn....\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.7,"y":18.9,"n":"Monika Sengutz","e":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"5531":{"id":5531,"t":"Betina Bigglezink","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Frozen Eggs to Betina Bigglezink.\nFrozen Eggs\nProvided: Frozen Eggs","desc":"The eggs you brought were to be used in Scourge experiments to create a plagued dragonflight. These frozen black dragon eggs would have been invaluable in their studies, and would have assuredly quickened their timetable.\nNow, it is time we ended their research.\nTake the frozen eggs to Betina Bigglezink outside. She is well-learned in science and alchemy, and has produced a weapon we can use against the Scourge. With your help, we will deal them a heavy blow.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Hello, ‹name›! I heard you were here with some dragon eggs? Well, let's see them!","done":"There they are! And in such a nice container. The perfect size!\nWe'll keep these eggs in a safe place so we can study them later, but right now we need that thing you brought them in.\nI have created a device with a very specific use: to destroy the undead scholars of the Scholomance. They are studying dragons in their efforts to create a plagued dragonflight, and we must halt their progress.\nI call the device Dawn's Gambit, because... I'm not sure if it works!\nWill you find out for us?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.3,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":49.9,"n":"Betina Bigglezink","e":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"1531":{"id":1531,"t":"Call of Air","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.","desc":"You be makin' headway now, mon. Your be ready to prove yerself worthy of the air totem, but first, ya must fin' Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles. She be willin' ta tell ya how to get yer air totem if ya treat her wit enough respect.\nHead south through the Barrens, and after ya reach Thousand Needles, head east. You'll find her hiddin' in a hole wit' her boyfriend--haha, don' tell her I be dissin' her none--she not take it too kindly.","rew":"You will receive:\nAir Totem\nExperience: 2,450","done":"For the time being. I shall give you what you need to focus your spells and to call upon the spirits of air. Take this totem, and when you are ready, train with me some more.\nOrgrimmar Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38,"y":37.7,"n":"Searn Firewarder","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":53.5,"y":42.6,"n":"Prate Cloudseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8411":{"id":8411,"t":"Mastering the Elements","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 52 instead of 50.","obj":"Bring the elements earth, air, fire and water to Bath'rah the Windwatcher.\nElemental Air Whirlwind Shredder 84.8 % , Whirlwind Stormwalker 83.7 % , Swirling Vortex 80 % , Whirlwind Ripper 79 % and 4 more\nElemental Earth Avalanchion 77.1 % , Baron Kazum 50.9 % , Rumbling Exile 11.1 % , Rock Elemental 11.1 % and 4 more\nElemental Fire Baron Charr 69.9 % , Prince Skaldrenox 42.7 % , Baron Geddon 30 % , Sulfuron Harbinger 30 % and 4 more\nElemental Water Princess Tempestria 73.9 % , Lord Skwol 46.7 % , Seeker Aqualon 26.9 % , Hydrospawn 26 % and 4 more","desc":"Welcome, ‹class›. You bring me the elements and then we do the talkin'.\nThe fire, the air, the water, and the earth I be needin' before I trust ya, mon. I gots to know you be knowledgeable.","rew":"Experience: 3,800","back":"Where's the elements, mon?","done":"These be the elements I need. Now we talk.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8331":{"id":8331,"t":"Aurel Goldleaf","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.","desc":"‹name›, although we had hoped the Twilight's Hammer's operations in Silithus were slowing... we were, regrettably, mistaken. Through continued forays against the cult, we have learned that an even darker power, the Abyssal Council, controls the Hammer through the arcane wind stones dotted amongst the cult's camps. Your next action, ‹name›, will be against the Abyssal Council.\nSpeak with the craftsman Aurel Goldleaf, in the eastern section of Cenarion Hold. Her skill will be needed for this next gambit.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"‹name›, good day. I was told you will pit yourself against the Abyssal Council? If that is so, then listen closely to my next words...","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.9,"n":"Huum Wildmane","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8731":{"id":8731,"t":"Field Duty","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Krug Skullsplit at the Orgrimmar Legion post in front of Hive'Regal. Prepare your Unsigned Field Duty Papers, obtain Signed Field Duty Papers and bring them to Windcaller Kaldon in Cenarion Hold.\nNote: Healing or casting beneficial spells on a member of the Orgrimmar Legion will flag you for PvP.\nSigned Field Duty Papers\nProvided: Unsigned Field Duty Papers","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›. Before I assign you to more involved tasks in the war, you'll need to do your share of field duty.\nYou will find Captain Skullsplit's Orgrimmar Legion outside Hive'Regal.\nReport to him and come back to me with proof of your field service. I shall have a more advanced assignment ready for you.\nOh, please do your best to stay away from the Ironforge Brigade. Tensions are high among our Alliance and Horde volunteers.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCombat Assignment Logistics Assignment Tactical Assignment\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You've completed your field duty, ‹name›? Captain Skullsplit can be found outside of Hive'Regal.","done":"I can tell that Krug has little use for paperwork. He signed this in silithid blood!\nVery well, ‹name›. I've prepared a set of tasks that should make good use of your skills as a ‹class›.\nWith the continued efforts of you and people like you, our enemy will soon be crushed!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50,"y":36.4,"n":"Windcaller Kaldon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"491":{"id":491,"t":"Wand to Bethor","lv":18,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Woven Wand to Bethor Iceshard in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\nWoven Wand\nProvided: Woven Wand","desc":"Thule once told me that, long ago, he and two colleagues created a magic wand, woven together from the apprentice wands each mage possessed. This wand was a symbol of their friendship, and although Thule came to despise it he could not part with it, nor could he let the others have it. So he stole the wand, and hid it in Fenris Keep.\nHere. Take the wand to Bethor Iceshard, one of Thule's friends from years past. I'm sure he will want it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nStamped Trousers Rugged Mail Gloves Serrated Knife\nExperience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"‹name›. Have you defeated Thule Ravenclaw?","done":"...what is this? Thule had our Woven Wand? I thought it was lost when our friendship sundered and he sided with the Lich King!\nHe must not have invoked its power, for if he had I would have sensed it. And it is good that he did not use it...\nThis is a marvelous find. You have my gratitude, ‹name›, and will be rewarded.\nSilverpine Forest Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":65.4,"y":24.8,"n":"Dusty Shelf","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":84.1,"y":17.4,"n":"Bethor Iceshard","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"171":{"id":171,"t":"A Warden of the Alliance","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return your ward to the Stormwind orphanage by handing in the Human Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Nightingale in the Cathedral District.\nHuman Orphan Whistle","desc":"You have been so very kind to me, ‹name›. I never dreamed that I'd have so much fun during Children's Week. Thank you. I don't wanna be sad about what's happened to me and all - my folks always told me to rise above anything bad that happens. You know, when I grow up I wanna be a hero... just like you.\nI'm sad to say this, but it's time for me to go home. Let's go back and I'll tell the matron what an awesome person you are!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPiglet's Collar Rat Cage Turtle Box Curmudgeon's Payoff\nExperience: 1,650\n+200 reputation with Alliance","back":"It is a pleasure to see you again, ‹name›. Have you attended to the duties you've volunteered for during Children's Week?","done":"May the heavens bless you, ‹name›. You've done more for Randis than most would ever think of doing for him. Thank you - you're a shining star in the skies of the Alliance.\nPlease - if you can spare the time, come back and visit us. I know that Randis would like that, as would I.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":56.3,"y":54,"n":"Orphan Matron Nightingale","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"331":{"id":331,"t":"Report to Doren","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lieutenant Doren.","desc":"Did Lieutenant Doren want you to report back to him with that patrol information?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nJunglewalker Sandals Frost Metal Pauldrons\nExperience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"It pains me to find out it was Merle who betrayed us. He has always been a brave soldier, and I had thought his heart was true. But it is a great relief to have found him out - with a spy like him among us...we would not last long against Colonel Kurzen.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":37.7,"y":3.4,"n":"Corporal Sethman","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3,"n":"Lieutenant Doren","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"571":{"id":571,"t":"Mok'thardin's Enchantment","lv":41,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Aged Gorilla Sinew to Far Seer Mok'thardin in Grom'gol.\nAged Gorilla Sinew Elder Mistvale Gorilla 5 %","desc":"What I need from you now will be very difficult to obtain.\nTo hold all these feathers, claws and the pristine fang in place I require a magical tether. Only an aged gorilla sinew will work.\nYou will only be able to find one on an Elder Mistvale Gorilla. They are known to forage to the east of Booty Bay.\nThe sinew must be perfect. It might take quite a few kills for you to find exactly what I need but it will be well worth the hunt.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Has fortune been on your side, ‹name›? Were you able to obtain an aged gorilla sinew?","done":"A most ideal sinew, ‹name›. Your efforts will pay off soon.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.1,"y":29.2,"n":"Far Seer Mok'thardin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1691":{"id":1691,"t":"More Wastewander Justice","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take down 10 Wastewander Shadow Mages, 8 Wastewander Rogues, and 6 Wastewander Assassins for Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan.\nWastewander Rogue slain : 0/ 8\nWastewander Assassin slain : 0/ 6\nWastewander Shadow Mage slain : 0/ 10","desc":"We need you to take on the stronger ranks of the Wastewander nomads now. You've done a good job thus far, but if we are to take back those water wells, then it only makes sense to do it against as few nomads as possible!\nThis time around we need you to take down their rogues, assassins, and shadow mages. You'll find them east and southeast of here.\nI'm not going to lie to you - they're a nasty lot. Do this for us though, and we'll be on our way to taking back what is rightfully ours!","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Well, were you able to take out those nomads like I asked? The Gadgetzan Water Company is developing plans based on your success here! Don't let us down, now...","done":"Top notch work, ‹name›... top notch! You've thinned down the nomad population to a point where we can actually take the fight to them!\nIf you haven't already, talk to Spigot Operator Luglunket here; he gives a bounty on any of the Wastewander water pouches you may have run across while bringing those nomads to justice!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"891":{"id":891,"t":"The Guns of Northwatch","lv":20,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun of Ratchet wants you to collect 10 Theramore Medals and slay Captain Fairmount, Cannoneer Whessan and Cannoneer Smythe.\n10 Theramore Medal Cannoneer Whessan 80 % , Cannoneer Smythe 80 % , Captain Fairmount 80 % , Theramore Preserver 80 % and 1 more\nCaptain Fairmount slain\nCannoneer Whessan slain\nCannoneer Smythe slain","desc":"Yet another ship from my fleet has been lost to those overzealous humans at Northwatch Hold!\nThose bastards must be dealt with. Their paranoia has them in a state of frenzy. Trigger happy, reckless louts are shooting at anything in their sights.\nTravel south along the Merchant Coast to the Hold and lay siege to their forces. Bring me the medals of their soldiers as proof. And for the love of my fleet, slay Captain Fairmount and her overzealous cannoneers!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPrivateer Musket Sea Dog Britches\nExperience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Ratchet\n+50 reputation with Horde","back":"My fleet is in peril with Captain Fairmount and her damned cannoneers blasting away from Northwatch Hold. I want her soldiers to pay as well. Fill my hand with medals from their dead and I will know that vengeance has been given to my fallen privateers.","done":"Alas, the righteous Alliance guns have been silenced. You shall be rewarded for your aid, ‹name›.\nNow to tend to the grim task of recovering the bodies of the dead....","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":39,"n":"Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1451":{"id":1451,"t":"Rhapsody Shindigger","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Rhapsody Shindigger in The Hinterlands.","desc":"Rhapsody took quite a liking to the booze. Now don't get me wrong -- all of us dwarves up here at the aviary love a good ale when the time is right.\nBut ol' Shindigger took to the liquor like a gryphon takes to the skies. And a damned shame it was, too. No one could fly like Rhapsody.\nFirst sign of trouble was when he came stumbling back from that mission with your buddy, Brohann. All went down hill quickly after that. Had to let him go.\nLast I heard, he's set up a brew camp to the east of here...","rew":"Experience: 1,800","done":"Hiccup!\nI'm a-lookin' right at you but you keep bobbing up and down. Makin' me dizzy. Hoho!\nHiccup!\nWhoa! Did ya feel that? Ground is a-shakin', my friend. I need a drink.\nHiccup!","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":9.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":26.9,"y":48.6,"n":"Rhapsody Shindigger","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"98251":{"id":98251,"t":"Never coming back","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 6 Shadowhorn Stag and 6 Ashenvale Bear and return to Va'xug Firefure northwest of Fallen Sky Lake.\nShadowhorn Stag slain : 0/ 6\nAshenvale Bear slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Gaaah!\nI'm so angry. They said Ashenvale was easy to follow. Easy for who? The beasts? The birds?\nOne moment I was gathering an herb, the next I'm trapped in this ravine. Do I truly have to circle half the forest to reach where I stood just moments ago?\nWhen I'm like this, my spells grow volatile and behave... differently.\nCould you thin the wildlife nearby? Even their stupid hooves grate on me. I despise this cursed forest.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff\nAshenvale Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":40.4,"y":61.4,"n":"Va'xug Firefure","s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"1131":{"id":1131,"t":"Steelsnap","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Steelsnap's Rib to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\nSteelsnap's Rib Steelsnap","desc":"At times we hunt for food. At times we hunt for honor. And at times we hunt to earn the Earthmother's teachings.\nBut the hunt I now set upon you is none of these things. It is to slay a creature outside the Earthmother's blessing.\nThe hyena Steelsnap roams the Thousand Needles, south of the Barrens. He is a tyrant, attracting other hyenas to him and spreading fear and bloodshed among more peaceful beasts.\nFind Steelsnap, ‹name›. Find him, and defeat him.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you defeated the foul Steelsnap, ‹name›?","done":"In defeating the creature Steelsnap, you have cleansed the Thousand Needles of a horrible taint.\nAnd that, ‹name›, is your lesson this day.\nThunder Bluff Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":61.5,"y":80.9,"n":"Melor Stonehoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"411":{"id":411,"t":"The Prodigal Lich Returns","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Nether Gem to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.\nNether Gem\nProvided: Nether Gem","desc":"Take this Nether Gem to my old comrade Bethor. It will let us communicate ... and I have much to tell him.","rew":"You will receive:\nBone Buckler\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you returned Gunther's book? Has he responded?","done":"You convinced him to join us! You have done a great deed for the Forsaken, ‹name›. The Dark Lady will be informed.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":68.2,"y":41.9,"n":"Gunther Arcanus","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":84.1,"y":17.4,"n":"Bethor Iceshard","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4491":{"id":4491,"t":"A Little Help From My Friends","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lead Ringo to Spraggle Frock at Marshal's Refuge.\nIf Ringo faints, use Spraggle's Canteen to revive him.\nProvided: Spraggle's Canteen","desc":"Ugh... It's so hot...\nI was exploring this area, when all of a sudden, the heat just became unbearable. I must be suffering from heat exhaustion.\nPlease, help me get back to my friend Spraggle at Marshal's Refuge. I think I'm well enough to follow you there.\nI am feeling a little out of it, so if I do happen to faint again, just splash some water on me from Spraggle's canteen. That should work, I hope...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBejeweled Legguards Treetop Leggings Clayridge Helm\nExperience: 5,650","back":"I've been so worried about Ringo...","done":"Ringo's not in the best shape, ‹name›, but I am glad to have him back in one piece!\nThank you for finding him.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":51.9,"y":49.8,"n":"Ringo","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.6,"y":8.5,"n":"Spraggle Frock","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"5051":{"id":5051,"t":"Two Halves Become One","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate the other half of the Good Luck Charm somewhere on the Felstone Farm in Western Plaguelands and reassemble it.\nGive the Good Luck Charm to Janice Felstone on the Felstone Farm, Western Plaguelands.\nGood Luck Charm\nProvided: Good Luck Half-Charm","desc":"The ramblings of the poor ghost continue:\n\"I'm so cold, John. Bring me your charm, and we'll be together! Quickly John, before the plague comes to change us into hideous beasts! I can't see you John... but I know you're near. I feel you near me.\"\nPerhaps if the second half of the charm was found and reassembled, this would constitute what the spirit of Janice Felstone is seeking.","rew":"You will receive:\nFelstone Good Luck Charm\nExperience: 5,450","back":"John, don't let the ghouls get you... don't let the ghouls get me... nasty ghouls... our charm will keep us safe.","done":"You hand the reassembled good luck charm to Janice Felstone's ghost. As soon as she grasps it, you observe an almost immediate change in her. Her ethereal form shimmers, and she looks upon you with clear yet sad eyes.\n\"You've freed me... I no longer will need this charm. Please, take it and perhaps it will give you the solace it has given me.\"","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":38.4,"y":54.1,"n":"Janice Felstone","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"4971":{"id":4971,"t":"A Matter of Time","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Temporal Displacer near one of Andorhal's silos and uncover Temporal Parasites.\nSlay 10 Temporal Parasites, and then return the Temporal Displacer to Chromie in the Andorhal Inn, Western Plaguelands.\nTemporal Displacer\nTemporal Parasite slain : 0/ 10\nProvided: Temporal Displacer","desc":"Tampering of the timeline by a sinister force - most likely the Scourge - has occurred in Andorhal! I can try to keep the passage of time here intact and mend what has been damaged, but I'll need your help to do so uninterrupted.\nTemporal parasites - carrion that feed on the strands of time's altered flow - now infest the silos of Andorhal. A blue pulse of distortion is their only visual marker. They slow my auguries; please ‹name›, help me by using this temporal displacer to root out these parasites.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOrchid Amice Gold Link Belt\nExperience: 5,800","back":"Temporal parasites are a common malady present wherever the flow of time has been tampered with. I sense that many are present, and this is disturbing.\nRooting out whatever ones you can find will help me be able to take a better hold on the deteriorating temporal situation here. I will be able to sense when this has been achieved.","done":"Time feels easier to mend now, thank you ‹name›. While you might not understand fully the consequences of a fractured timeline, I appreciate that you understand the urgency of countering what I suspect more and more to be a Scourge-driven malfeasance.\nI see no harm in rewarding you for your assistance, mortal. Your greatest feats are to come, and the awarding of a bauble will certainly not alter your future destiny. Your continued aid, however, is something that I and the dragonflight could use...","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"94411":{"id":94411,"t":"Meddlesome mages","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 6 High Order Apprentices in Shen'dar Highlands.\nHigh Order Apprentice defeated : 0/ 6","desc":"Be warned, members of the High Order have been seen in the vicinity of the standing stones north of the village. We have warned them time and again to not meddle at our sacred sites, but they are growing more bold in pushing us. Prove your resolve to us by going to the standing stones and dispersing them.\nI am loathe to condone outright bloodshed, but do what you must to drive them off. Return to me when its done.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIdol of Shifting Tides\nMoney: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 410\n+100 reputation with Windshapers","done":"Direct conflict with our shen'dorei brothers and sisters only weakens us as a people, but decisive action must at times be taken to prevent greater tragedy.\nThe mages of the High Order have zero regard for the consequences of their magical meddling. The forces that bind our island are fragile and vulnerable and all it could take is one thoughtless action to destroy our home.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Illaya Amberwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94491":{"id":94491,"t":"The fate of the den","lv":12,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valannar and tell him what has transpired.\nMysterious Orders","desc":"It would appear that there is a correspondent hiding somewhere in Valanaar feeding information to the cult. I am clearly in no shape to make the journey, but Lotheluum needs to know what transpired here.\nHe should also know the fate of those who are no longer with us. Thanks to your help I think we can handle the rest of the situation from here, thought the damage has been done.\nPlease go swiftly, ‹name›. I hope our paths will cross again someday. Until then, I have cultists to slay.","done":"<Lotheluum wears a look of genuine terror as you recount the events from the ‹class› den.>\nI--I'm sorry, Solarus. I need just a moment. There are no words I possess that can describe the loss.\nThis is grave news indeed. If this missive is not fabricated, then we indeed have at best an accomplice and at worst a traitor here in Valanaar. I will take this to the High Elder immediately! I will not let my fellows sacrifice be in vain.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":64,"y":75,"n":"Lotheluum Starbreeze","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});